WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:14.970
Last time: green flag · move · turn

3
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.930
Unit 3 · Building With Blocks

4
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:23.380
Chapter 3 · Variables

5
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:31.280
How does a game remember your score?

6
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:37.000
Let's find out the secret!

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.250
Riya plays a coin game in the auto

8
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:56.380
Coin! Score 0 → 1 → 2 → 3

9
00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:04.950
Spike! Lives 3 → 2

10
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:15.670
Where does the game keep these numbers?

11
00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:24.480
In a named box, called a VARIABLE

12
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:34.870
Var · i · a · ble → it can change

13
00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:45.610
A named box that holds one value

14
00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:57.630
Name outside · Value inside

15
00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:03.390
Name: score · Value: 5

16
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:09.720
Your tiffin box has a name label

17
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:17.710
Label = whose box · Inside = lunch

18
00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:26.400
Mon poha · Tue paratha · Wed idli

19
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:36.690
Same name, changing value = variable

20
00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:41.420
Games are full of variables

21
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:47.410
score · counts points · starts at 0

22
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:53.520
lives · chances left · like 3

23
00:02:53.520 --> 00:03:05.850
name · holds a word, like "Riya"

24
00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:16.070
Screen glass, charger → not variables

25
00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:22.830
Two variable blocks: set and change

26
00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:31.740
set score to 0 → the box now holds 0

27
00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:39.730
Set at the start → every game starts fresh

28
00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:50.170
change score by 1 → 5 becomes 6

29
00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:59.810
change score by −1 → 6 becomes 5

30
00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:05.160
Good names, bad names

31
00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:18.510
x1 · box · abc → what's inside?

32
00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:31.200
stars · lives · score → short and clear

33
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:42.650
Best name for counting stars?

34
00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:50.610
stars! Clear names help people

35
00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:55.650
Detective time: follow the score box

36
00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:10.050
set 0 · coin · coin · coin · bug

37
00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:18.450
What is the score at the end?

38
00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:33.180
0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 2. The score is 2!

39
00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.060
Your turn: practice check

40
00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:49.100
3 lives. Hit a spike. Lives become…?

41
00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:59.480
change lives by −1 → 3 − 1 = 2

42
00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:09.010
Bonus: 3 lives, 2 spikes. Lives = ?

43
00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:18.280
3 → 2 → 1. One life left!

44
00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:23.970
Variable = a named box with a value

45
00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:30.590
It can change · numbers or words

46
00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.610
+1 goes up · −1 goes down

47
00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:39.940
Clear names: stars, not x1

48
00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:47.510
Chapter 3 done!

49
00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:54.310
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
